                <pb facs="0182" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/19<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >12/14</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-22T14:00:00-03:30">October 22, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 22—1:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>241. Your 93, August 4, 3 p.m. Lieutenant Colonel Christian and Captain Brereton
                    arrived this morning and we had a satisfactory preliminary meeting with the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, the Minister of National Defense and the Inspector
                    General of the Navy.</p>
                <p>The conversations with officers of the Uruguayan Army and Navy will begin
                    tomorrow morning.</p>
                <p>Please advise General Strong.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
